{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Execution status — session paused for handoff (session log `d999-072a-be04-493e`)\n\nClaimed and in progress. **Plan review PASSED** after **8 passes**; attestation certified. The plan changed materially during those passes — anyone implementing a child should re-read the epic description rather than working from memory of it.\n\n### Substantive plan defects found and fixed (all verified against the code, not taken on faith)\n\n1. **Three acceptance criteria were literally truncated mid-sentence** (`...selected by`, `...sanitizers,`, `...written before any`) — unverifiable as written. Rewritten as observable end-states.\n2. **The plan ignored ADR 0035 §(a)'s location-pinned files.** `adf.py`, `outbound_fields.py`, and `comment_limits.py` are loaded **by path** and the pin is live (`inbound_fields.py:36`; `outbound_fields.py:69`; `tests/.../state/test_config.py:193`; `tests/integration/.../test_reconcile_roundtrip.py:72`; `tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py:121`; ~9 test files for `comment_limits`). Moving them would have broken the dynamic loader **silently**. Resolution: **share by dependency inversion, not relocation** — and the key distinction the plan had conflated is that *location-pinned means the file cannot change PATH, not that it cannot be EDITED*.\n3. **The value maps were already duplicated AND already drifted** — found independently by a mutation that failed to go red, and corroborated by the reviewer. There are **three** copies of the status map; two agree on `deleted -> Done`, and only the ACLI-side copy omits it, producing `\"Deleted\"` — **not a state in the live DIG workflow**, so Jira would reject that transition. J2 now single-sources the maps in `jira_family/` and adopts `deleted -> Done` as **the one declared observable change** in an otherwise behavior-preserving story.\n4. **`jira_fields.py` cannot move wholesale** — it imports from **two** pinned modules (`adf.py` via `_sanitize_description`, `comment_limits.py` via `_sanitize_comment`), so moving it would invert the epic's own import contract. Resolution: **move by SYMBOL**, with the two coupled sanitizers **parameterized by the `RichTextCodec`/comment-limit contracts** the epic already introduces.\n5. **Two contradictions I introduced myself, then fixed:** my TLS requirement would have rejected J5's own `http://localhost:2990` harness (resolved by making the harness the intended `allow_insecure` case, with the reject branch unit-tested on a non-loopback URL); and an \"exactly one dict literal **across the whole engine**\" AC contradicted my own deferral of `config.py`'s third copy (AC narrowed to `adapters/`).\n\n### Coverage gaps closed by pushing parent ACs down into children\n\nTLS enforcement + `ca_bundle` + `resolved_statuses` -> **J6**; the reciprocal `jira_datacenter` import check and adding `jira` to the clean-core CI list -> **J7** (verified: `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml:108` lists only 5 modules, so the \"no new dependency\" AC had **no CI teeth**); operator PAT/CA/resolved-statuses docs -> **J8**; the machine-checked import contract -> **J2**, with the mechanism **chosen** (an AST-walking test inside `make test`, matching existing practice in `test_backend_neutrality.py:25,107,110`) rather than left as \"import-linter or equivalent\".\n\nAlso: `classify_probe_response` now takes the resolved-status set **as a parameter** — its hardcoded `{Resolved, Done, Cancelled}` are Cloud/DIG names, and sharing them verbatim would misclassify a **resolved** DC issue as `PRESENT_FILTERED`.\n\n**Empirically settled (not assumed):** absolute `from rebar_reconciler...` imports resolve fine under `spec_from_file_location` loads with `__package__ == ''`, because the conftest puts the engine dir on `sys.path`. A **relative** import would raise there. Recorded in J2 as a hard constraint.\n\n### Child state at pause\n\n| Story | Status | Plan review |\n|---|---|---|\n| J1 `acb2` | in_progress, work done, **Gerrit 1009 awaiting votes** | certified |\n| J2 `62d9` | open — description heavily rewritten | unsigned; blocked until J1 closes |\n| J3 `aac8` | open — codec seam aligned with J2 | unsigned; blocked |\n| J4 `0a94` | open, untouched | unsigned; blocked |\n| J5 `c97f` | open — **CLAIMABLE NOW**, independent | **PASSED + certified** |\n| J6 `9fd4` | open — TLS/ca_bundle/resolved_statuses ACs added | unsigned; blocked |\n| J7 `b4e3` | open — import check + clean-core CI ACs added | unsigned; blocked |\n| J8 `8c35` | open — operator-docs AC extended | unsigned; blocked |\n\nDiscovered work: bug `fe15-3bc4-ed70-4b61`, linked `discovered_from` J1.\n\n**The tree is strictly serial by design:** `review-plan` fast-fails `INDETERMINATE` (no LLM spend) on any ticket whose prerequisites are unclosed, so children cannot be pre-reviewed. **J5 is the only parallel work available.**"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338251317222001,"uuid":"862f6d2a-8f7f-4096-b042-37b82d78ce43"}